[list]
[*]The seven floor border buttons have left the Floors tab, where they sat among the floors. They are at the end of the Misc tab now, after everything else there. The hard edge marker is still on Floors.
[*]With Better Architect Menu, which has no Misc tab, they get a Trims section of their own on its Decorate tab. If you have added, removed or dragged sections on Decorate in that mod's edit mode, its saved list has no Trims section, so the buttons go to its Miscellaneous section under World. Add Trims to Decorate with the edit mode's + button, and they move there the next time you open the Architect.
[*]To have them on Floors again, untick [b]Put the floor borders on the Misc tab[/b] in Neat Edges' mod settings. With Better Architect Menu the box reads [b]Put the floor borders under Decorate, in a Trims section[/b]. The buttons move at once, in a running game too.
[*]A note at the main menu says all this once, with a button that puts them back on Floors.
[*]Unchanged: Neat Edges still requires only Harmony, and nothing new is saved in your games; the mod settings file holds the box and which note you have closed. Borders, markers and hard edge areas already in your saves load as they are. The one def added is the Trims section, which loads only with Better Architect Menu.
[/list]
